{
  "summary": "Reported: Dana Whitfield (CEO, VIP, user_id 1) got a new iPhone yesterday and Duo pushes no longer arrive, so VPN is blocked. She needs VPN for a board prep call at 2:00 PM ET today. Time-sensitive.\nChecked: The account is active, not locked, sign-in not blocked, VPN access enabled, 0 failed logins. Duo is enrolled (duo_push, registered to 'Duo Mobile on Dana's phone', enrolled 2025-12-13), so it is still tied to the old phone. Laptop BL-LT-0101 is online with no warnings. Sign-in logs for 14 days: 9 successful sign-ins, all New York, within usual hours, no mfa_denied, no unrequested pushes, no hosting networks. Last VPN success was Thu 10/08 08:07 ET. Nothing suspicious.\nNeeded (KB-004 new phone): verify identity by calling back the number on file, then reactivate Duo Mobile on the new iPhone and send a test push. Tier 1 has no tool to reactivate Duo. The request came from her verified company email. If she cannot be verified by callback, do not reactivate.",
  "reason": "KB-004 new-phone Duo reactivation needs a callback identity check and a Duo reactivation that Tier 1 tools can't do. VIP user with a deadline at 2 PM."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for the details. Your account looks fine. Duo is still linked to your old phone, so the new iPhone needs to be set up in its place. I've passed this to our Tier 2 team as urgent and told them about your 2:00 PM call. To confirm it's you, someone will call you back on the phone number we have on file. Then they'll help you activate Duo on your new iPhone and send a test push. To save time, install the Duo Mobile app from the App Store now if you haven't already. Until Duo is set up on the new phone, VPN won't connect. If you still have the old phone and it's working, approving pushes on it may get you through for now.",
  "internal_note": "VIP/CEO, P2, VPN needed for a 2 PM ET board prep call. Account active, not blocked, VPN access on, 0 failed logins. Duo enrolled (duo_push) but still tied to the old phone. Laptop BL-LT-0101 online, no warnings. 14 days of sign-ins: all successful from NY within usual hours, no MFA denials or unrequested pushes, no sign of compromise. Under KB-004 (new phone), Duo needs reactivation after a callback to the number on file. Tier 1 has no Duo reactivation tool, so I escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) for the callback and reactivation. Request came from her verified company email.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-004",
    "KB-013"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
